1
00:00:00,112 --> 00:00:02,187
This is RadeonNav.

2
00:00:02,276 --> 00:00:07,021
A quadruped that plans its route around what its own skills can and cannot do,

3
00:00:07,101 --> 00:00:11,601
running entirely on an AMD Radeon GPU with ROCm.

4
00:00:12,301 --> 00:00:13,021
The task:

5
00:00:13,101 --> 00:00:17,246
a twenty-eight by ten metre serpentine course, nine obstacle segments,

6
00:00:17,326 --> 00:00:20,821
and the robot is given nothing but a few sparse route anchors,

7
00:00:20,901 --> 00:00:25,163
no predefined dense waypoints, no obstacle labels.

8
00:00:25,340 --> 00:00:30,115
Which skill to fire, and which way to go, it must decide on its own.

9
00:00:30,842 --> 00:00:33,800
Three open-source projects make up the stack.

10
00:00:33,880 --> 00:00:35,887
NeuPAN provides the planning core,

11
00:00:35,967 --> 00:00:39,992
a real-time point-cloud planner with a learned distance field.

12
00:00:40,176 --> 00:00:43,896
Quadrupedal-agility provides the frozen locomotion skills,

13
00:00:43,976 --> 00:00:46,996
natural behaviours learned from canine motion capture,

14
00:00:47,076 --> 00:00:50,176
plus the depth encoder we fine-tune.

15
00:00:50,360 --> 00:00:53,705
And UniLab is the ROCm-native simulation framework

16
00:00:53,785 --> 00:00:57,510
the whole system is rebuilt and evaluated in.

17
00:00:57,976 --> 00:01:01,183
Our contribution is the layer that makes them one system:

18
00:01:01,263 --> 00:01:04,408
single-obstacle tests measure what the skills can cross,

19
00:01:04,488 --> 00:01:06,271
the planner routes around the rest,

20
00:01:06,351 --> 00:01:10,446
and task classes along the route fire the right skill at the right place;

21
00:01:10,526 --> 00:01:12,858
only the depth encoder is retrained,

22
00:01:12,938 --> 00:01:16,701
in under ninety seconds, on planner-collected data.

23
00:01:17,584 --> 00:01:21,559
Now the course, one continuous rollout, no cuts.

24
00:01:21,732 --> 00:01:26,957
Rough terrain, stairs, a hinged seesaw, all taken in stride.

25
00:01:29,628 --> 00:01:33,065
Between tasks the planner handles the turns alone.

26
00:01:37,748 --> 00:01:40,148
A crawl through the elevated tunnel.

27
00:01:44,812 --> 00:01:47,869
This hurdle exceeds the policy's jumping ability,

28
00:01:47,949 --> 00:01:51,974
so the planner detours, yielding to a pedestrian on the way.

29
00:01:56,177 --> 00:02:00,014
The tire hoop, a committed heading, and straight through the ring.

30
00:02:04,217 --> 00:02:07,655
Four poles, left, right, left, right.

31
00:02:10,336 --> 00:02:15,574
Two crossing pedestrians, and done, zero collisions, zero falls.

32
00:02:16,444 --> 00:02:19,801
Now the same fixtures, four strategies side by side:

33
00:02:19,881 --> 00:02:23,589
the planner alone, top left, detours everything;

34
00:02:23,669 --> 00:02:28,214
the teacher, top right, runs on privileged, hand-authored inputs;

35
00:02:28,294 --> 00:02:32,726
the onboard student, bottom left, red frame, never arrives;

36
00:02:32,806 --> 00:02:37,906
and ours, bottom right, same frozen networks, new interface.

37
00:02:38,600 --> 00:02:42,808
The pole line, only the privileged teacher can weave the one-metre gaps;

38
00:02:42,888 --> 00:02:45,850
ours knows it cannot, and routes around.

39
00:02:46,536 --> 00:02:50,799
The hoop, only ours and the privileged teacher actually make the jump.

40
00:02:51,460 --> 00:02:53,392
And the hurdle tells the whole story.

41
00:02:53,472 --> 00:02:58,167
At ten centimetres the released teacher jumps it, the deployable student stalls:

42
00:02:58,247 --> 00:03:02,272
the skill exists in the weights, not in the onboard form.

43
00:03:02,448 --> 00:03:04,605
At full height nobody clears it;

44
00:03:04,685 --> 00:03:10,560
ours is measured on that form, so it never gambles, it detours, and arrives.

45
00:03:11,424 --> 00:03:14,174
Reproducing this takes two commands.

46
00:03:14,260 --> 00:03:19,323
One prepares the ROCm environment and verifies the Radeon GPU.

47
00:03:20,012 --> 00:03:24,932
One runs the full course and writes the rollout video and a machine-checkable verdict,

48
00:03:25,012 --> 00:03:27,700
every check true, goal reached.

49
00:03:28,568 --> 00:03:33,124
RadeonNav, skill-aware navigation with natural behaviours.

50
00:03:33,204 --> 00:03:37,374
Sixty percent faster on traversable terrain than planning alone,

51
00:03:37,454 --> 00:03:43,317
teacher-level outcomes with no privileged inputs, all on a single Radeon GPU.

52
00:03:43,484 --> 00:03:48,084
Code, report, and every run record are in the repository.

53
00:03:48,581 --> 00:03:50,043
Thanks for watching.

